  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Proxies and Load Balancers: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Proxies and Load Balancers: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Forward vs Reverse Proxy",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Forward proxy==: speaks for **clients**; server sees the proxy's IP",
                "Uses: egress control, filtering, caching, hiding client IPs",
                "==Reverse proxy==: speaks for **servers**; client sees one public address",
                "Uses: TLS termination, routing, caching, compression"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Forward",
                "Reverse"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Configured by",
                  "Client",
                  "Server owner"
                ],
                [
                  "Job",
                  "Controls clients",
                  "Scales servers"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Load Balancer",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Load balancer== = reverse proxy that spreads requests over a pool",
                "Goal: no single server is the bottleneck or single point of failure"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "ink": "black"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Virtual IP",
                    "sub": "floating",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "LB pair",
                    "sub": "active-passive",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Backend pool",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Calling every proxy a load balancer",
                "One load balancer is not highly available"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Make it HA",
              "text": "Run an ==active-passive== or active-active pair behind a floating **virtual IP**."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Forward vs reverse?** Forward serves clients; reverse serves servers.",
                "**Is one LB highly available?** No; use a pair with a virtual IP.",
                "**Proxy vs LB?** An LB is a reverse proxy that spreads load."
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "L4 vs L7 Load Balancing",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "L4 vs L7 Load Balancing",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What each layer sees",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:L4}: routes on ==src/dst IP and port==, payload unread",
                "Very fast, protocol-agnostic (any TCP/UDP)",
                "One client connection maps to ==one backend connection=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{purple:L7}: parses HTTP, routes on ==host, path, header, cookie, method==",
                "Also terminates TLS, rewrites headers, retries, compresses",
                "Costs more CPU"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "L4",
                "L7"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Sees",
                  "IPs and ports",
                  "URL, headers, cookies"
                ],
                [
                  "Path routing",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "{green:Yes}: /api and /static pools"
                ],
                [
                  "Cookie stickiness",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Speed",
                  "Fastest",
                  "Slower"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Real products",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "L4",
                "L7"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "AWS",
                  "**NLB**: static IP, millions of conn/s",
                  "**ALB**: host/path rules"
                ],
                [
                  "nginx",
                  "`stream` block",
                  "`http` block"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "L7 in front of long-lived non-HTTP traffic (database, raw TCP)",
                "L4 chosen while expecting path-based routing"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Client IP is lost behind L7",
              "text": "The balancer replaces the client IP. Read ==X-Forwarded-For== or enable ==PROXY protocol== to get the real one."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Balancing Algorithms, Health Checks and Sticky Sessions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Balancing Algorithms, Health Checks and Sticky Sessions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Picking a Backend",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Algorithm",
                "Picks",
                "Best for"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Round robin",
                  "next in order",
                  "similar request cost"
                ],
                [
                  "Weighted RR",
                  "bigger servers get more turns",
                  "mixed server sizes"
                ],
                [
                  "Least connections",
                  "fewest active connections",
                  "variable or long-lived requests"
                ],
                [
                  "IP / consistent hash",
                  "fixed backend per client or key",
                  "affinity; consistent hash: few remaps"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Health Checks",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Probe",
                    "sub": "GET /healthz on an interval",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "3 failures",
                    "sub": "mark unhealthy",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "2 passes",
                    "sub": "restore",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Active==: probe on an interval, expect `200`",
                "==Passive==: eject a backend after real request errors"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Sticky Sessions",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pin via ==cookie== (L7) or ==source-IP hash== (L4)",
                "Skews balance; session lost if backend dies",
                "Prefer stateless: sessions in ==Redis== or a ==JWT=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Port-only check, or `200` while the database is down",
                "Deep check hitting the DB from every balancer: whole pool drops",
                "No ==connection draining== (deregistration delay): in-flight requests cut on deploy"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Check real readiness, not too deep; drain before removal."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "CDN Edge Caching and Anycast",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "CDN Edge Caching and Anycast",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Edge Caching",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "sub": "asks nearest edge",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Edge",
                    "sub": "HIT: serve",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Origin",
                    "sub": "MISS: fetch",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Store",
                    "sub": "next request hits",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cache-Control and Cache Key",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Directive",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`max-age`",
                  "browser and CDN TTL"
                ],
                [
                  "`s-maxage`",
                  "shared caches, CDN"
                ],
                [
                  "`public` / `private`",
                  "CDN may store / browser only"
                ],
                [
                  "`no-store`",
                  "never cache"
                ],
                [
                  "`stale-while-revalidate`",
                  "serve stale, refresh in background"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Cache key== = host + path + query string",
                "Add `Vary` or cookies only if needed: each part lowers the ==hit ratio==",
                "Versioned names `app.9f3a.js` allow a year-long `max-age` with `immutable`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
              ],
              "note": "for versioned assets"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Anycast",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Anycast==: one IP prefix announced from many sites via **BGP**",
                "Routers deliver to the nearest site: low latency",
                "Site withdraws its route: automatic failover",
                "DDoS traffic is absorbed across sites",
                "{orange:Geo-DNS} instead returns different IPs by resolver location"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Caching personalized or `Set-Cookie` responses publicly",
                "No purge after a deploy: use versioned URLs instead",
                "Long TCP flows on anycast: a route change can move them mid-connection"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Everyday Commands and Config",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Everyday Commands and Config",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. nginx pool and real client headers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==upstream== is the pool; `proxy_pass` points at it",
                "`weight` gives bigger servers more turns; `max_fails` ejects"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "nginx",
              "lines": [
                "upstream app {",
                "  least_conn;",
                "  server 10.0.0.1:8080 weight=3;",
                "  server 10.0.0.2:8080 max_fails=3 fail_timeout=30s;",
                "}",
                "location / { proxy_pass http://app; }"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "`proxy_set_header`",
                "Value"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Host",
                  "`$host`"
                ],
                [
                  "X-Real-IP",
                  "`$remote_addr`"
                ],
                [
                  "X-Forwarded-For",
                  "`$proxy_add_x_forwarded_for`"
                ],
                [
                  "X-Forwarded-Proto",
                  "`$scheme`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. HAProxy backend and stickiness",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`check` runs the health probe; `fall 3` down, `rise 2` up",
                "==cookie SRV insert== pins a client; `cookie s1` names the server"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "haproxy",
              "lines": [
                "backend app",
                "  balance leastconn",
                "  option httpchk GET /healthz",
                "  cookie SRV insert indirect nocache",
                "  server s1 10.0.0.1:8080 check inter 2s fall 3 rise 2 cookie s1"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Inspect and trust",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command / field",
                "Tells you"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`curl -I https://site/asset`",
                  "Cache-Control, Age"
                ],
                [
                  "X-Cache, cf-cache-status",
                  "==HIT== or MISS"
                ],
                [
                  "Via",
                  "proxy hops"
                ],
                [
                  "`curl --resolve site:443:ORIGIN_IP https://site/`",
                  "tests origin directly"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Spoofable X-Forwarded-For",
              "text": "Never use a client-sent value for access control or rate limits. Trust only what your own proxy appended; set the ==trusted proxy list== explicitly."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
